    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Along the Moab-Spanish Valley, Utah, normal faults in the Jurassic Entrada Fm sandstone have developed by contributions from (1) deformation banding overprinted by (2) jointing and shearing along joints. Overprinting contributions by each deformation mechanism to faulting have resulted in complex fault and damage zones. The fault architecture resulting from these mechanisms correlates with the relative timing and the proportion of offset each deformation mechanism accommodates.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
